      "text": "67-year-old female presenting with headache with dizziness for 2 weeks. Character: throbbing at the back of the head; radiation: it does not spread; aggravated by morning time; relieved by rest. Severity 8/10. Associated: palpitations, blurred vision. PMH: Hypertension for 14 years. Drugs: Amlodipine 5 mg. Allergy: no known allergies. Family: no similar illness. Personal: non-smoker, no alcohol. Triage: URGENT."
